cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "Pairwise Poisson Algebras of the N-Body Problem"
abstract: >-
  Symbolic and numerical computation of the Lie algebra generated by pairwise
  interaction Hamiltonians of the N-body problem under the Poisson bracket.
  Establishes the dimension sequence [3, 6, 17, 116, 5914] for N=3
  (last term a certified mod-p lower bound, equality with high
  probability) and its universality across potentials, spatial
  dimensions (through level 3), mass ratios, and charge magnitudes;
  extends to N=4 ([6, 14, 62, 1260]), N=5 ([10, 25, 145, 5965]) and
  higher N at level 2; cross-CAS verified in SymPy, Wolfram Language
  and SageMath.
